Subject: [PATCH 2/8] [AI] Store amounts at the same x100 scale for every
 currency

Zero-decimal currencies such as yen were scaled by 10^decimalPlaces in
useFormat and some util helpers, while the rest of the code used x100.
A 1,500 yen budget showed as 15 on one screen and 150,000 on another.

Amounts are now always stored x100; a currency's decimal places only
affect display. amountToInteger, integerToAmount and integerToCurrency
no longer take a decimalPlaces argument, and the callers that passed
currency.decimalPlaces as a scale are updated. The legacy AmountInput
skips autoDecimals for currencies without decimals.

The INTEGER_TO_AMOUNT formula still accepts its optional second argument
so saved formulas do not error, but ignores it. It is removed from the
formula catalog and docs.

