@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+---
+category: Bugfix
+authors: [context-ops-demo]
+---
+
+Store amounts at the same scale for every currency, so zero-decimal currencies like yen no longer show as 15 on one screen and 150,000 on another (the `INTEGER_TO_AMOUNT` formula's optional second argument is now ignored; it still divides by 100)

From 9c300f541fad3a3f7526e931e264e8e7497f3c0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Context Ops Demo <demo@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:09:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] [AI] Use undici's fetch throughout the sync server

SimpleFIN passed an undici v8 Agent as the dispatcher to Node's built-in
global fetch, which bundles a different undici version. Import fetch from
undici in every sync server module (SimpleFIN, CORS proxy, GoCardless,
Enable Banking, health check) so the dispatcher and fetch always match.

Tests now mock undici's fetch instead of the global one, and a new
SimpleFIN integration test exercises the real fetch and SSRF dispatcher
against a local HTTP server. Raise the sync server Node floor to 22.19.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
